       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.      TPARMINQ.
       AUTHOR.          JEFF BUNGO.
       DATE-WRITTEN.    JULY 15, 1997.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      ***************************************************************
      ************ THIS PROGRAM CONTAINS SQL STATEMENTS   ***********
      ************ USE CRTCBLSQL COMMIT(*NONE) RDB(*NONE) ***********
      ************ TO CREATE THE PGM OBJECT.              ***********
      ***************************************************************

      ***************************************************************
      *  PROGRAM TO ALLOW CODE PARAMETER INQUIRIES                  *
      *                                                             *
      *  AN SQL STATEMENT IS BUILT TO RETRIVE CODES THAT HAVE A     *
      *  MATCH ANYWHERE IN ITS DESCRIPTION TO A GIVEN VALUE.        *
      *  THESE CODES WILL BE LISTED WITH KEYWORD/MODIFIER AND       *
      *  AND 1ST LINE OF DESCRIPTION.  A CODE MAY THEN BE SELECTED  *
      *  FOR MATERIAL STATUS INQUIRY.                               *
      ***************************************************************
DP9802*C  27FEB1998      DAVE PLUM                                  *
DP9802*C    ADDED LOGIC TO INITIALIZE THE BU-PGM-NAME FIELD.        *
DP9806*C                                                            *
DP9806*C  08JUN1998      DAVE PLUM                                  *
DP9806*C    REVISED TO CORRECT AN ERROR INVOLVING THE WRITE OF THE  *
DP9806*C    SUBFILE ("ERROR ON SHOW SPL WRITE").  IF AFTER          *
DP9806*C    WRITING THE SUBFILE TO THE SCREEN, THE USER PRESSED     *
DP9806*C    ENTER WITHOUT MODIFYING ANY OF THE RECORDS (DID NOT     *
DP9806*C    SELECT ANY CODE FOR Q1) THEN THE "READ NEXT MODIFIED"   *
DP9806*C    STATEMENT RESULTED IN AN INVALID RELATIVE RECORD NUMBER.*
DP9806*C    THIS LED TO AN ERROR WHEN CONTROL TRANSFERRED BACK TO   *
DP9806*C    THE 63-PROCESS-SUBFILE PARAGRAPH.                       *
DP0003*C                                                            *
DP0003*C  23MAR2000      DAVE PLUM                                  *
DP0003*C    REVISED TO IMPROVE THE TBLOWUP INFORMATION PROVIDED     *
DP0003*C    WHEN AN ERROR OCCURS WRITING THE SFL RECORD.  ALSO      *
DP0003*C    ATTEMPTED TO ELIMINATE THESE ERRORS BY LIMITING THE     *
DP0003*C    NUMBER OF CODES RETRIEVED TO 9,998.  (THE SUBFILE       *
DP0003*C    SEEMS TO ONLY BE ABLE TO HANDLE 9,999 RECORDS.  UPON    *
DP0003*C    WRITING THE 9,999TH RECORD TO THE SUBFILE A STATUS OF   *
DP0003*C    "9M" IS RETURNED.)                                      *
      ***************************************************************
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       COPY SPECIALN IN COPYLIB.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT DISPLAY-FILE
                  ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-ZPARMINQ-SI
                  ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
                  ACCESS IS DYNAMIC
                  RELATIVE KEY IS RELATIVE-RECNO
                  FILE STATUS IS DISPLAY-STATUS
                  CONTROL-AREA IS WS-CONTROL.
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  DISPLAY-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
       01  DISPLAY-REC        PIC X(2000).

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
      *
      * SQL COMMUNICATIONS AREA
      *
       77  CODE-EDIT                     PIC ---99.
       77  SQL-FUNCTION                  PIC X(20).
       77  NUM-CODES-PER-SCREEN          PIC 9(1) VALUE 9.
       01  STRING-STATUS                 PIC X(1) VALUE "N".
           88  END-OF-STRING                      VALUE "Y".
           88  NOT-END-OF-STRING                  VALUE "N".
       01  SQL-STATUS-CODES  COMP-4.
           05 GOOD-CALL    VALUE 0    PIC S9(4).
           05 NOT-FOUND    VALUE 100  PIC S9(4).
           05 CONV-ERROR   VALUE 304  PIC S9(4).
           05 MAP-ERROR    VALUE 802  PIC S9(4).
           EXEC SQL   INCLUDE SQLCA   END-EXEC.
       01  FILE-STATUS                   PIC X(2).
       01  LANG-FLAG                     PIC X(1) VALUE "P".
           88  PRIMARY                            VALUE "P".
           88  SECONDARY                          VALUE "S".

      *
      * MISC. DATA DECLARATIONS.
      *
       01  SUB                           PIC 99.
       01  SEARCH-VALUE-CHARACTER.
           05  SEARCH-VALUE-CHAR OCCURS 80 TIMES PIC X(1).
       01  CODES-RETRIEVED               PIC 9(5).
       01  DIVIDEND                      PIC 9(5).
       01  REMAIN                        PIC 9(5).

      *
      * INCLUDE TABLE DEFINITIONS
      *
           EXEC SQL   BEGIN DECLARE SECTION   END-EXEC.

       01  DDESC-STRUCTURE.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCS1401.

       01  SEARCH-STRING                    PIC X(82).
       01  SEARCH-VALUE.
           49  SEARCH-VALUE-SIZE            PIC S9(2) COMP-4.
           49  SEARCH-VALUE-PARM            PIC X(80).

           EXEC SQL   END DECLARE SECTION   END-EXEC.

      *
      * SCREEN DATA
      *

       COPY IOFEEDBACK IN COPYLIB.
       COPY DISPDATA IN COPYLIB.
       01  RELATIVE-RECNO               PIC 9(9).

       01  ENTRY-SCREEN.
           05  SEARCH-CRITERIA           PIC X(80).
           05  DE-COMMAND-LINE-1         PIC X(79).
           05  DE-MESSAGE                PIC X(79).

       01  SUBFILE-RECORD.
           05  SFC-RCDNBR                PIC 9(4).
           05  SFC-SEARCH                PIC X(79).
           05  SFL-RECORD.
               10  SEL                   PIC X(1).
               10  V-CODE                PIC X(7).
               10  V-KWM                 PIC X(50).
               10  V-DESC                PIC X(80).

       01  BUF-LINES.
           05  BUF-LINE-1                PIC X(79).
           05  BUF-LINE-2                PIC X(79).

DP0003 01  ERROR-MSG-TOO-MANY.
DP0003     05  FILLER  PIC X(22) VALUE "MORE THAN 9,998 CODES ".
DP0003     05  FILLER  PIC X(28) VALUE "MEET THIS SEARCH CRITERIA.  ".
DP0003     05  FILLER  PIC X(26) VALUE "PLEASE ENTER NEW CRITERIA.".
DP0003     05  FILLER  PIC X(3)  VALUE SPACES.
      *
      * SUBPROGRAM AREA
      *
       01  BASE                          PIC X(10).
       01  CODE-ARG                      PIC X(8).
       01  TMTLSTAT-PARAMETERS.
           05  TMTLSTAT-COMPANY          PIC X(4) VALUE SPACES.
           05  TMTLSTAT-CODE             PIC X(7) VALUE SPACES.
       01  PASSED-SPOOL-PRT              PIC S9(2) COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       COPY CDESC IN COPYLIB.
       COPY CATREAD IN COPYLIB.
       COPY VCOMAREA IN COPYLIB.
       COPY LANGUAGE IN COPYLIB.
       COPY TBLOWUP IN COPYLIB.
       COPY DBSTAT IN COPYLIB.


       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-LINE-LOGIC.

           PERFORM 1-HOUSEKEEP THRU 1-EXIT.
           PERFORM 6-MAIN THRU 6-EXIT.
           GOBACK.

       1-HOUSEKEEP.
DP9802     MOVE "TPARMINQ" TO BU-PGM-NAME.
           OPEN I-O DISPLAY-FILE.
           INITIALIZE ENTRY-SCREEN.
           INITIALIZE SUBFILE-RECORD.
           INITIALIZE BUF-LINES.
       1-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       6-MAIN.
           PERFORM 61-ENTER-SEARCH THRU 61-EXIT.
           IF FUNCTION-NUM = "03"
               GO TO 6-EXIT.
           PERFORM 62-RETRIEVE-CODES THRU 62-EXIT.
           IF CODES-RETRIEVED = 0
               MOVE "NO CODES MEET SEARCH CRITERIA" TO DE-MESSAGE
               MOVE B"1" TO IND(99)
               GO TO 6-MAIN.
DP0003
DP0003******* SINCE THE SUBFILE CAN ONLY HANDLE 9,998 RECORDS, IF THIS
DP0003******* MANY CODES HAVE BEEN RETRIEVED WE WILL DISPLAY AN ERROR
DP0003******* MESSAGE.   ---DAVE PLUM 23MAR2000
DP0003     IF CODES-RETRIEVED = 9998
DP0003         MOVE ERROR-MSG-TOO-MANY TO DE-MESSAGE
DP0003         MOVE B"1" TO IND(99)
DP0003         GO TO 6-MAIN.
DP0003
           MOVE 1 TO SFC-RCDNBR.
           PERFORM 63-PROCESS-SUBFILE THRU 63-EXIT.
           GO TO 6-MAIN.
       6-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       61-ENTER-SEARCH.
           MOVE ENTRY-SCREEN TO DISPLAY-REC.
           WRITE DISPLAY-REC FORMAT IS "PARMINQ"
              INDIC ARE SRF-INDICATORS.
           MOVE ALL B"0" TO SRF-INDICATORS.

           READ DISPLAY-FILE FORMAT IS "PARMINQ"
              INDIC ARE SRF-INDICATORS.
           ACCEPT IOFEEDBACK FROM I-O-FEEDBACK-AREA.
           MOVE DISPLAY-REC TO ENTRY-SCREEN.
           MOVE ALL B"0" TO SRF-INDICATORS.
           IF DISPLAY-STATUS NOT = "00"
              MOVE "03" TO FUNCTION-NUM.
           IF FUNCTION-NUM NOT = "00" AND NOT = "03"
              AND NOT = "01"
              MOVE 9 TO LANG-SETNUM
              MOVE 10 TO LANG-MSGNUM
              MOVE 09010 TO CATREAD-MSG-NUMBER
              PERFORM 999-CATREAD THRU 999-CATREAD-EXIT
              MOVE B"1" TO IND(99)
              GO TO 61-ENTER-SEARCH
           ELSE
              IF FUNCTION-NUM NOT = "03"
                IF SEARCH-CRITERIA = SPACES
                  MOVE 20 TO LANG-SETNUM
                  MOVE 62 TO LANG-MSGNUM
                  MOVE 20062 TO CATREAD-MSG-NUMBER
                  PERFORM 999-CATREAD THRU 999-CATREAD-EXIT
                  MOVE B"1" TO IND(99)
                  GO TO 61-ENTER-SEARCH.
           IF FUNCTION-NUM = "01"
              SET SECONDARY TO TRUE
           ELSE
              SET PRIMARY TO TRUE.
       61-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       62-RETRIEVE-CODES.
      *-------CLEAR SUBFILE
           PERFORM 622-CLEAR-SUBFILE THRU 622-EXIT.
      *-------PARSE ENTERED STRING, DELIMITING WITH 2 SPACES
      *-------  WILD CARD SYMBOLS ARE ADDED TO STRING BEGINING AND END
           MOVE SPACES TO SEARCH-VALUE-PARM.
           STRING "%" DELIMITED BY SIZE
                  SEARCH-CRITERIA DELIMITED BY "   "
                  "%" DELIMITED BY SIZE
              INTO SEARCH-VALUE-PARM.

      *------COMPUTE THE SEARCH SIZE FOR VARIABLE LENGTH FIELD
           MOVE SPACES TO SEARCH-VALUE-CHARACTER.
           MOVE SEARCH-VALUE-PARM TO SEARCH-VALUE-CHARACTER.
           MOVE 0 TO SEARCH-VALUE-SIZE.
           SET NOT-END-OF-STRING TO TRUE.
           PERFORM VARYING SUB FROM 1 BY 1
              UNTIL END-OF-STRING
                IF SUB > 2
                  IF SEARCH-VALUE-CHAR(SUB - 1) = "%"
                      SET END-OF-STRING TO TRUE
                  ELSE
                      ADD 1 TO SEARCH-VALUE-SIZE
                  END-IF
                ELSE
                  ADD 1 TO SEARCH-VALUE-SIZE
                END-IF
           END-PERFORM.
      *    DISPLAY "SEARCHING FOR "
      *            SEARCH-VALUE-PARM(2:SEARCH-VALUE-SIZE - 2).

      *------BUILD SQL STATEMENT
           MOVE SPACES TO SEARCH-STRING.
           IF PRIMARY
               STRING "SELECT DISTINCT CORPCDE FROM MCFLCS1401 WHERE "
                      "DESCDTA LIKE ?" DELIMITED BY SIZE
                  INTO SEARCH-STRING
           ELSE
               STRING "SELECT DISTINCT CORPCDE FROM MCFLCS3101 WHERE "
                      "DESCDTA LIKE ?" DELIMITED BY SIZE
                  INTO SEARCH-STRING
           END-IF.
           EXEC SQL   PREPARE S1 FROM :SEARCH-STRING
           END-EXEC.
           IF SQLCODE < 0
              MOVE "PREPARE" TO SQL-FUNCTION
              PERFORM 20-BLOWUP.

      *------DECLARE SQL CURSOR
           EXEC SQL   DECLARE C1 CURSOR FOR S1
           END-EXEC.
           IF SQLCODE < 0
              MOVE "DECLARE CURSOR" TO SQL-FUNCTION
              PERFORM 20-BLOWUP.
           EXEC SQL   OPEN C1 USING :SEARCH-VALUE  END-EXEC.
           IF SQLCODE < 0
              MOVE "OPEN CURSOR" TO SQL-FUNCTION
              PERFORM 20-BLOWUP.

      *---------GET FIRST CODE BY FETCHING CURSOR
           EXEC SQL   FETCH C1 INTO :MCRPCS1400.CORPCDE
           END-EXEC.
           IF SQLCODE < 0
              MOVE "FIRST FETCH" TO SQL-FUNCTION
              PERFORM 20-BLOWUP.

      *---------FETCH REST OF CODES UNTIL END
           MOVE 0 TO CODES-RETRIEVED
                     RELATIVE-RECNO.
           PERFORM UNTIL SQLCODE NOT EQUAL ZERO
DP0003       OR CODES-RETRIEVED IS EQUAL TO 9998
               ADD 1 TO CODES-RETRIEVED
      *        DISPLAY CORPCDE OF MCRPCS1400
      *----------GET KWRD/MOD AND 1ST LINE OF DESCRIPTION FOR CODE
               PERFORM 621-GET-CODE THRU 621-EXIT
      *----------WRITE TO SUBFILE
               MOVE SPACES TO SEL
               ADD 1 TO RELATIVE-RECNO
               WRITE SUBFILE DISPLAY-REC FROM SFL-RECORD
                  FORMAT IS "PARMSF"
                  INDICATORS SRF-INDICATORS
               END-WRITE
               IF DISPLAY-STATUS NOT = "00"
                   MOVE "ERROR WRITING SFL RECORD" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
                   MOVE DISPLAY-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS
DP0003             MOVE CODES-RETRIEVED TO BU-DISPLAY-FLD9 (1)
DP0003             MOVE RELATIVE-RECNO  TO BU-DISPLAY-FLD9 (2)
                   PERFORM 2100-BLOWUP
               END-IF

      *----------GET NEXT CODE
               EXEC SQL   FETCH C1 INTO :MCRPCS1400.CORPCDE
               END-EXEC
               IF SQLCODE < 0
                  MOVE "FETCH" TO SQL-FUNCTION
                  PERFORM 20-BLOWUP
               END-IF
           END-PERFORM.

      *-------CLOSE CURSOR
           EXEC SQL   CLOSE C1   END-EXEC.
       62-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       621-GET-CODE.
           MOVE 2                        TO   CDESC-LINES-TO-GET.
           MOVE LANG-FLAG                TO   CDESC-LANGUAGE-OPTION.

           MOVE "D"                      TO   CDESC-DESC-OPTION.
           MOVE "N"                      TO   CDESC-LOCAL-DESC-OPTION.
           MOVE CORPCDE OF MCRPCS1400    TO   V-CODE
                                              CODE-ARG.
           CALL "CDESC" USING CDESC-RET-CODE, BASE, STATUS-AREA,
             BU-DISPLAY-MSG, CODE-ARG, CDESC-DATA.
           IF BU-DISPLAY-MSG-1 NOT = SPACES
               MOVE CDESC-RET-CODE TO FILE-STATUS
               PERFORM 2100-BLOWUP.
           MOVE CDESC (1) TO   V-KWM.
           MOVE CDESC (2) TO   V-DESC.
       621-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       622-CLEAR-SUBFILE.
           MOVE B"1" TO IND(71)
                        IND(72)
                        IND(73).
           WRITE SUBFILE DISPLAY-REC FROM SUBFILE-RECORD
              FORMAT IS "PARMSFC"
              INDICATORS ARE SRF-INDICATORS.
           MOVE B"0" TO IND(72).
       622-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       63-PROCESS-SUBFILE.
           WRITE DISPLAY-REC FROM BUF-LINES
             FORMAT IS "PARMFUNC"
             INDICATORS ARE SRF-INDICATORS.
           MOVE SEARCH-CRITERIA TO SFC-SEARCH.
           MOVE ALL B"0" TO SRF-INDICATORS.
           MOVE B"1" TO IND(70)
                        IND(71)
                        IND(73).

DP9806*------ 08JUN1998 ADDED LOGIC TO INSURE THAT THE SUBFILE
DP9806*------  RECORD NUMBER IS NOT LESS THAN 1.
DP9806     IF SFC-RCDNBR < 1
DP9806         MOVE 1 TO SFC-RCDNBR.

           WRITE SUBFILE DISPLAY-REC FROM SUBFILE-RECORD
              FORMAT IS "PARMSFC"
              INDICATORS ARE SRF-INDICATORS.
           IF DISPLAY-STATUS NOT = "00"
               MOVE "ERROR ON SHOW SFL WRITE" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
               MOVE DISPLAY-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS
               PERFORM 2100-BLOWUP.
           MOVE ALL B"0" TO SRF-INDICATORS.
           MOVE B"1" TO IND(70)
                        IND(71)
                        IND(73).
           READ DISPLAY-FILE
              FORMAT IS "PARMSFC"
              INDICATORS ARE SRF-INDICATORS.
           IF DISPLAY-STATUS NOT = "00"
               MOVE "ERROR ON SFL READ" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
               MOVE DISPLAY-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS
               PERFORM 2100-BLOWUP.
           IF FUNCTION-NUM = "03"
              GO TO 63-EXIT.

           READ SUBFILE DISPLAY-FILE NEXT MODIFIED RECORD
              FORMAT "PARMSF"
              INDICATORS ARE SRF-INDICATORS
DP9806        AT END
DP9806            MOVE 1 TO SFC-RCDNBR
DP9806            GO TO 63-PROCESS-SUBFILE.

           IF DISPLAY-STATUS = "12"
              COMPUTE SFC-RCDNBR =
                 RELATIVE-RECNO / (NUM-CODES-PER-SCREEN + 1)
              COMPUTE SFC-RCDNBR =
                 SFC-RCDNBR * NUM-CODES-PER-SCREEN
              DIVIDE NUM-CODES-PER-SCREEN INTO SFC-RCDNBR
                 GIVING DIVIDEND REMAINDER REMAIN
              IF REMAIN = 0
                 ADD 10 TO SFC-RCDNBR
              ELSE
                 ADD 1 TO SFC-RCDNBR
              END-IF
              GO TO 63-PROCESS-SUBFILE.
           MOVE DISPLAY-REC TO SFL-RECORD.
           IF SEL NOT = SPACES
              MOVE SPACES TO SEL
              MOVE SFL-RECORD TO DISPLAY-REC
              REWRITE SUBFILE DISPLAY-REC
                FORMAT IS "PARMSF"
                INDICATORS ARE SRF-INDICATORS
              END-REWRITE
              MOVE V-CODE TO TMTLSTAT-CODE
              CALL "TMTLSTAT" USING BASE
                                    VIEW-COMAREA
                                    TMTLSTAT-COMPANY
                                    PASSED-SPOOL-PRT
                                    TMTLSTAT-CODE
                                    LANGUAGE-PARMS
              DIVIDE NUM-CODES-PER-SCREEN INTO RELATIVE-RECNO
                 GIVING DIVIDEND REMAINDER REMAIN
              IF REMAIN > 0
                  COMPUTE SFC-RCDNBR =
                    NUM-CODES-PER-SCREEN * DIVIDEND + 1
              ELSE
                  COMPUTE SFC-RCDNBR =
                    NUM-CODES-PER-SCREEN * DIVIDEND
                     - (NUM-CODES-PER-SCREEN - 1)
              END-IF
              GO TO 63-PROCESS-SUBFILE.

       63-EXIT.
           EXIT.


      ***************************************************************
      * PARAGRAPH : 20-BLOWUP                                       *
      * PURPOSE   : TO ABORT THE PROGRAM AND DISPLAY ERROR MESSAGE  *
      ***************************************************************
       20-BLOWUP.
           MOVE SQLCODE TO CODE-EDIT.
           DISPLAY "PROGRAM = TPARMINQ".
           DISPLAY "AN SQL ERROR HAS OCCURRED SQLCODE = "
                   CODE-EDIT ":" SQL-FUNCTION.
           DISPLAY SQLERRMC.
           GOBACK.

       2100-BLOWUP.
           MOVE V-CODE TO BU-DISPLAY-FLD(1).
           CALL "TBLOWUP" USING BASE, BU-PGM-NAME, STATUS-AREA,
                 VIEW-COMAREA, FILE-STATUS, BU-DISPLAY-MSG,
                 BU-DISPLAY-AREA.

       999-CATREAD.
           IF CATREAD-MSG-NUMBER = ZEROS
               MOVE LANG-SETNUM TO CATREAD-MSG-SET
               MOVE LANG-MSGNUM TO CATREAD-MSG-NUM.
           CALL "CCATREAD" USING CATREAD-PARMS.
           MOVE CATREAD-MSG-TEXT TO DE-MESSAGE.
       999-CATREAD-EXIT.
           EXIT.
